    [
      "RL-18151 receiving and interpretation",
      [
        "Original values and limits remain separate. Recognized left-censored rows have [0, published limit) when their positive limit and result units match. If both original result value and unit are blank, an explicitly published positive limit retains its own separate unit and original_quantitation_limit basis. Conflicting nonblank units and unknown conditions retain no numeric interval. No half-limit substitution.",
        "Annual summaries retain exact characteristic, fraction, units, medium, depth, method and result-basis cohorts. Different cohorts are not pooled.",
        "Original lake sampling concentrations and physical measurements are contextual observations. No annual catchment export, discharge or load is inferred.",
        "Original narrow ResultIdentifier binds each record. Exact shared default-profile fields, unique Activity metadata and native ResultIdentifier limits select retained source candidates. Indistinguishable full-profile row positions remain explicit candidate sets; original result identities are never collapsed.",
        {
          "kind": "links",
          "items": [
