    [
      "RL-18151 sampling support and activity sensitivity",
      [
        "498 original results remain attached to 40 original activities. The 83 exact source cohorts remain available beside 66 explicitly compatible measurement cohorts.",
        "Separate source cohorts remain unchanged. Compatible measurement summaries require exact agreement on selected year, characteristic, fraction, quantitative unit inherited from the maintained interval, chemical basis, medium, activity type, both sampling depths and references, analytical method/context/name, result basis, time/weight/temperature/particle basis, statistical base, qualifier and status. Original unit and interval-unit provenance are retained as complete member sets within every compatible cohort. No chemical conversion, missing-depth substitution or cross-year pooling is performed.",
        "Equal-activity means average each activity's original result intervals, then weight activities equally. Result-weighted means weight every original assay equally. Difference bounds retain each unknown censored value in both estimands. These are descriptive interval bounds, not sampling confidence intervals.",
        "The compatible review retains 31 repeated activity/cohort groups; 31 have agreeing quantitative values. Metadata agreement is shown separately. No original identifier is collapsed.",
        {
          "kind": "table",
          "columns": [
            "Year",
            "Depth",
            "Results",
            "Activities",
            "Equal-activity phosphorus bounds",
            "Unit / chemical basis"
